---
description: Type-safe, idempotent TypeScript with clear JS/TS names
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# TypeScript

- Keep `strict` mode. No `any`. Prefer `unknown` + narrowing. Avoid `as` except beside a runtime check.
- `interface` for object shapes (models, props). `type` for unions, intersections, aliases.
- Export explicit parameter and return types. Name domain types (`DrugCandidate`), not anonymous objects.

```ts
// ❌
function label(d: any) { return d.name }

// ✅
function getCandidateLabel(candidate: DrugCandidate): string {
  return candidate.name.trim();
}
```

# Naming

- PascalCase for classes, types, interfaces, and React components. camelCase for values and functions. kebab-case for files (not PascalCase filenames).
- `useX` hooks; `is`/`has`/`can` booleans; `handleX` handlers; `onX` callback props.
- Names describe meaning. No `tmp`, `data1`, `IDrug`, `strName`.

# Idempotent FP

- Pure functions: same inputs → same outputs. Never mutate arguments or module state; return new values.
- I/O stays at edges. Domain logic must be safe to re-run.
- DRY: extract shared knowledge (filters, mappers). Do not abstract accidental JSX similarity.
- Prefer `map`/`filter`/early returns over mutating loops.

```ts
// ❌ candidates.forEach(c => { c.status = "approved" })
// ✅ candidates.map(c => ({ ...c, status: "approved" as const }))
```
